1
00:00:02,560 --> 00:00:04,360
<i>The sign…</i>

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:09,160
<i>The sign…</i>

3
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:11,320
<i>The sign…</i>

4
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:16,360
<i>There will be certain signs</i>
<i>that only we can perceive.</i>

5
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:27,880
Happy birthday, my mystic heir.

6
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:28,880
Mom!

7
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:40,320
Congratulations, sweetheart.
You're the next heir!

8
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:43,120
<i>It's time!</i>

9
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:47,400
No!

10
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:58,200
It's not my birthday yet, right?

11
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:02,880
Hello?

12
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:05,400
Grandma called.

13
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:09,120
Here.

14
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:11,480
Hello, Ms. Jomkwan.

15
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:13,960
Why are you still awake this late?

16
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:17,200
Hello, Danthai.

17
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:18,880
No, Grandma.

18
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:21,160
It's Rin, not Danthai.

19
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:23,640
Hello, Grandma.

20
00:01:23,720 --> 00:01:25,360
<i>Oh? Then whose voice was that?</i>

21
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:27,280
Is that your boyfriend, Rin?

22
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:29,440
Grandma, no.

23
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:32,520
That was Danthai, my cousin.

24
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:34,040
<i>Right.</i>

25
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:36,360
The heir to our family's mystical lineage?

26
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:40,760
Like anyone actually wants that.

27
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:42,240
Huh? What?

28
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:45,760
<i>You think being the family mystic</i>
<i>means an easy life? Huh? Right?</i>

29
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:48,040
Being the family mystic
means an easy life?

30
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:49,840
<i>Not a chance.</i>

31
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:51,400
But you must become one.

32
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:53,400
You must become one!

33
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:57,240
You must become one!

34
00:01:57,320 --> 00:02:00,560
<i>Once you come of age and are chosen,</i>
<i>that's what you'll become.</i>

35
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:01,600
<i>That's how it is.</i>

36
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:05,680
Grandma, it's time for your medicine.

37
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:09,120
Nurse.

38
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,760
Please cut Ms. Jomkwan's Internet.
Otherwise, she'll never go to bed tonight.

39
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:15,800
Sleep well. Bye.

40
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:18,320
<i>Love you, sweetheart.</i>

41
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:20,760
- Love you, Ms. Jomkwan.
- Love you, Ms. Jomkwan.

42
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:25,040
I'm sorry, man.

43
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:27,960
It was an emergency.
I had to use your bathroom to poop.

44
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:30,880
What's wrong? Why do you look like that?

45
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:38,600
My birthday isn't today, right?

46
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:41,280
Are you okay?

47
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:46,280
<i>And this is Rin,</i>

48
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:48,520
<i>a second-year Fine Arts student,</i>
<i>majoring in painting.</i>

49
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:50,240
<i>He's the star of the Fine Arts Faculty</i>

50
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:53,400
<i>who's been winning drawing competitions</i>
<i>since elementary school.</i>

51
00:03:53,480 --> 00:03:55,480
<i>You could say he's perfect in every way.</i>

52
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:57,680
<i>Good looks, talent,</i>

53
00:03:57,760 --> 00:04:01,080
<i>and to top it off, he's got two equally</i>
<i>fabulous best friends, like us two!</i>

54
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:03,840
OHM, BESTIE NUMBER 1

55
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:06,400
JINNIE, BESTIE NUMBER 2

56
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:09,480
<i>And here's the second-year Fine Arts gang.</i>

57
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:12,720
<i>Basically, we're top-notch,</i>

58
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:14,400
<i>but as if that wasn't enough,</i>

59
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:19,720
<i>Rin's perfect boyfriend is Krit,</i>
<i>the Business Faculty's Moon.</i>

60
00:04:20,760 --> 00:04:24,840
<i>Seriously, how can one person have it all?</i>

61
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:26,120
<i>I'm so envious!</i>

62
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:32,920
I'm so talented! Awesome.

63
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:34,680
Hey!

64
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:36,560
Are you done editing yet?

65
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:39,400
We're going to be late.
We'll have Prof. James next.

66
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:41,280
He'll roast us alive.

67
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:43,880
Yes. It's done.

68
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:45,840
It's your fault anyway.
You don't upload clips often.

69
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:49,200
- Huh?
- I have to film you and edit your clips.

70
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:52,200
I'm just protecting your follower count.
What's wrong with that?

71
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:53,800
So somehow that's my fault?

72
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:56,640
Crap!

73
00:04:56,720 --> 00:05:00,280
I forgot my EE pencil sharpener.

74
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:02,600
See? You're forgetful.

75
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:05,280
You're always forgetting something,
literally everything.

76
00:05:05,360 --> 00:05:07,400
- Serves you right.
- You never stop nagging.

77
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:11,080
Relax. I brought an extra.

78
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:15,480
Thanks a lot, Rin.

79
00:05:17,840 --> 00:05:20,160
Now that's what I call a real friend.

80
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:23,400
And you're the worst!

81
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:24,960
Let's go already.

82
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:27,280
Oh, wait…

83
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:31,000
I forgot my carbon eraser.

84
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:34,560
See? And you're always nagging me.

85
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:35,800
I'm allowed to forget stuff too.

86
00:05:35,880 --> 00:05:37,680
- Like you've never forgotten anything.
- There you go again.

87
00:05:37,760 --> 00:05:39,480
- You--
- Here.

88
00:05:40,160 --> 00:05:41,600
I brought an extra for you too.

89
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:44,280
Thanks, buddy.

90
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:47,720
They don't call him
"Perfect Rin" for nothing.

91
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:05,040
<i>Mom, how could you know it was time</i>
<i>to become the next mystic heir?</i>

92
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:06,880
<i>The sign…</i>

93
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:10,800
<i>There will be certain signs</i>
<i>that only we can perceive.</i>

94
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:46,240
What are you looking for?

95
00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:49,800
A guitar sound. Do you guys hear it?

96
00:06:49,880 --> 00:06:51,520
- No.
- No.

97
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:08,240
<i>The sign…</i>

98
00:07:08,320 --> 00:07:09,760
<i>Congratulations, sweetheart.</i>

99
00:07:09,840 --> 00:07:12,400
<i>You're the next heir!</i>

100
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:14,560
<i>It's time!</i>

101
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:35,000
<i>The sign…</i>

102
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:37,680
<i>The sign…</i>

103
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:42,000
<i>There will be certain signs</i>
<i>that only we can perceive.</i>

104
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:48,320
<i>Okay, class dismissed.</i>

105
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:49,680
See you next session.

106
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:51,400
- Thanks, Professor!
- Thank you.

107
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:53,360
Bye. Bye, guys.

108
00:07:56,760 --> 00:07:58,560
- Damn, I was so tense.
- Yeah, very much.

109
00:07:58,640 --> 00:07:59,760
Here.

110
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:01,720
Thank you.

111
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:03,720
Rin, my bestie.

112
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:05,320
Thanks, bro.

113
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:06,920
Anytime.

114
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,600
So you're really not eating with us today?

115
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:10,720
I really can't.

116
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:13,480
I made plans to meet Krit
in front of the faculty ages ago.

117
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:14,640
Next time, okay?

118
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:17,680
Look at you,
all clingy with your boyfriend.

119
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:19,000
That's annoying!

120
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:21,720
Well, at least I have
a boyfriend to cling to.

121
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:24,600
Did you really have to rub that in?

122
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:27,800
Jinnie, that's not showing off.
I'm actually seeing someone too.

123
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:30,200
We just haven't made
our status official yet.

124
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:32,679
Everyone in this group is taken,
except you.

125
00:08:32,760 --> 00:08:34,840
And how do you know I'm single?

126
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:38,200
I just don't tell nosy people like you!

127
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:42,240
Sure. I'll do my best to believe it.

128
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:49,000
<i>My class is almost done. See you.</i>

129
00:08:52,760 --> 00:08:54,000
<i>See you.</i>

130
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:56,080
I'm off. See you later.

131
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:57,120
Yes, see you.

132
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:58,760
- Bye.
- Bye.

133
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:06,080
Yo, bae!

134
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:14,120
Huh?

135
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,160
Hey!

136
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:37,920
How much was your coffee?
I'll pay you back.

137
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,520
Did you forget something?

138
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:43,480
What?

139
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:46,440
I mistook you for someone else
and spilled your coffee.

140
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:48,200
So let me pay for it.

141
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:51,640
Come on, show me your QR code.
I'll transfer it.

142
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:53,120
Hey.

143
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:55,400
"Yo, bae!"

144
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,520
Seriously? Do you think I'm a joke to you?

145
00:09:58,600 --> 00:10:00,560
Who raised you? Mocking people like that?

146
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:05,440
Hold on. I'm not done talking.

147
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:06,760
Do you have any manners?

148
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:11,280
Hey, where do you think you're going?

149
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:14,040
No one's ever ignored me like this.

150
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:18,760
Guess I'm your first.

151
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:26,720
You… You!

152
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:30,600
Come back here!
I'm not done yelling at you!

153
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:31,760
Where are you going?

154
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:33,200
Hey!

155
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:37,240
Rin, have you been waiting long?

156
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:40,720
The professor kept me after class.

157
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:44,080
Why do you look like that?

158
00:10:44,160 --> 00:10:45,160
I'm hungry.

159
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:54,800
So that guy's really your friend?

160
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:57,240
Yes. Same year.

161
00:10:57,840 --> 00:10:59,080
We're not close, though.

162
00:11:00,320 --> 00:11:03,040
I don't think
you should get involved with him.

163
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:05,960
Why? We don't need to be scared of him.

164
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:09,600
People in the faculty say he's trouble.

165
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:12,320
He's already bad enough today.
He could act worse?

166
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:13,840
They say he's kind of weird too.

167
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:17,240
I heard he caused another fight recently.

168
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:22,520
Like beating people up?

169
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:40,600
They say Khobfa snatched a girl's bag

170
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:44,880
and tried to extort her.

171
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:47,920
Hand me the bag!

172
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:51,040
No! Give it back! Let go!

173
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:52,840
What are you doing? Ow!

174
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:00,360
He's seriously the worst.

175
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:04,800
Whoever dates him is cursed for life.

176
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:09,840
Krit, promise me you'll never get involved
with that thug. Got it?

177
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:12,320
I don't usually talk to him anyway.

178
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:14,320
Good.

179
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:15,720
Well…

180
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:18,320
I forgot.

181
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:20,800
You said you wanted to tell me
something today.

182
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:22,040
Yes.

183
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:27,520
Well, I…

184
00:12:32,040 --> 00:12:32,960
I…

185
00:12:33,880 --> 00:12:35,440
You?

186
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:36,880
I think…

187
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:38,520
What?

188
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:42,000
I think…

189
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:43,320
What?

190
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:44,680
Rin! Krit!

191
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:47,560
Can we take pictures with you?
We're so happy to meet you in person.

192
00:12:58,400 --> 00:12:59,400
- Thank you.
- Thanks.

193
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:07,800
I'm exhausted.

194
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:10,760
That afternoon class killed me.

195
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:13,440
Three straight hours
of standing there painting!

196
00:13:13,520 --> 00:13:15,160
I'm done.

197
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:18,600
Guys. Let's film a story.

198
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:22,040
No way.

199
00:13:22,120 --> 00:13:26,320
Look at my face.
I look half-dead and sleepy.

200
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:28,840
Rin, my buddy.

201
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:31,680
Help me out here, okay?

202
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:35,320
People keep DMing me
asking why you don't post often.

203
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:38,160
I just don't care much about this stuff.

204
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:40,480
If I post all the time,
it's not cool anymore.

205
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:41,520
Damn.

206
00:13:42,080 --> 00:13:43,480
That's freaking fab.

207
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:47,680
What? Move.

208
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:51,680
<i>Hello! Fit check!</i>

209
00:13:51,760 --> 00:13:55,240
<i>Today's look is casual streetwear,</i>
<i>looking comfy and colorful.</i>

210
00:13:55,320 --> 00:13:57,960
<i>This oversized tee pairs well with jeans,</i>

211
00:13:58,040 --> 00:14:00,840
<i>while accessories</i>
<i>complete the streetwear look.</i>

212
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:05,040
- Hey.
- Damn.

213
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:07,040
Who's that, Jinnie?

214
00:14:07,120 --> 00:14:09,720
Mochi, a Communication Arts student.

215
00:14:09,800 --> 00:14:10,960
He's blowing up right now.

216
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:13,800
Everything he touches
turns into a viral hit.

217
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:16,560
He's got 300,000 Instagram followers.

218
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:18,400
He's landed over a hundred review deals.

219
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:21,480
Shit. That's insane.

220
00:14:21,560 --> 00:14:22,720
Rin.

221
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:25,600
Didn't he go to the same school
as Krit and you?

222
00:14:26,880 --> 00:14:27,920
Do you know him?

223
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:32,760
Well, I used to.

224
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:35,120
But we're not really close anymore.

225
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:41,200
Yes, but damn, the editing's really good.

226
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:43,600
He has so many followers.

227
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:48,920
<i>Promise we'll stay friends forever.</i>

228
00:14:49,920 --> 00:14:52,400
Never break the group's rules.

229
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:56,000
- No dating within the group. Ever.
- No dating within the group. Ever.

230
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:57,160
Deal?

231
00:14:57,240 --> 00:14:58,240
Deal.

232
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:03,840
- Yay!
- Yay!

233
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:20,320
Krit asked me out after we graduated.

234
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:23,520
I didn't break our promise.

235
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:29,280
<i>Where is Krit?</i>

236
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:31,480
He doesn't know I'm taking this class.

237
00:15:31,560 --> 00:15:32,920
I'm here to surprise him.

238
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,760
Yes, sir.

239
00:15:35,920 --> 00:15:37,200
Sure, sure.

240
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:42,680
<i>I heard he caused another fight recently.</i>

241
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:50,120
<i>Khobfa snatched a girl's bag</i>
<i>and tried to extort her.</i>

242
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:53,280
What the hell?

243
00:15:58,400 --> 00:15:59,240
He's here.

244
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:07,120
Huh?

245
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:09,440
He totally walked right past you.

246
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:12,560
While you're glowing this much.

247
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:16,920
What are you waiting for? Go say hi.

248
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:18,200
- Go on.
- Hurry up.

249
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:20,360
Okay, welcome, everyone,

250
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:25,040
to this semester's course,
Natural Plants and Environment!

251
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:28,160
Okay.

252
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:30,920
Let's take a look at the course handout

253
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,600
and see what we'll be studying
this semester.

254
00:16:33,680 --> 00:16:34,640
Okay.

255
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:39,440
This is the handout.

256
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:42,280
It corresponds with
the research over there.

257
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:44,520
Take a look at the research.

258
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,760
<i>Are you seeing what I'm seeing?</i>

259
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:10,319
<i>I am. Rin, do you see it?</i>

260
00:17:15,480 --> 00:17:18,240
<i>It's nothing. They know each other.</i>

261
00:17:18,319 --> 00:17:19,920
