519
00:43:56,640 --> 00:43:57,640
No.

520
00:43:58,960 --> 00:44:00,240
Ex-besties, actually.

521
00:44:05,720 --> 00:44:07,640
So you're doing this to get back at me?

522
00:44:07,720 --> 00:44:09,040
If you're saying that,

523
00:44:09,120 --> 00:44:10,760
it means you knew all along.

524
00:44:10,840 --> 00:44:13,760
You knew you betrayed me when you broke
our rule about no dating within the group.

525
00:44:14,440 --> 00:44:16,040
I didn't break the rule.

526
00:44:16,120 --> 00:44:17,720
We made it in high school.

527
00:44:17,800 --> 00:44:19,840
Krit asked me out after we graduated.

528
00:44:19,920 --> 00:44:21,160
Enough, Rin.

529
00:44:21,840 --> 00:44:24,880
I only came here to clear this up. Okay?

530
00:44:25,920 --> 00:44:28,120
It's not okay.
Who the hell would be okay with this?

531
00:44:28,200 --> 00:44:29,080
Of course.

532
00:44:29,160 --> 00:44:31,800
You're the type who always has to win.
You can't stand losing, can you?

533
00:44:32,400 --> 00:44:35,000
- Me?
- Yes, you.

534
00:44:36,040 --> 00:44:39,160
Then how about this?

535
00:44:39,800 --> 00:44:43,680
This semester, let's compete. You and I.
We'll compete through activities.

536
00:44:43,760 --> 00:44:45,720
Whoever has more followers
by the end of the semester wins.

537
00:44:45,800 --> 00:44:47,840
What the hell? What does that
even have to do with anything?

538
00:44:47,920 --> 00:44:50,320
Why? Are you scared?

539
00:44:51,160 --> 00:44:54,120
Who's scared?
Follower count? That's nothing.

540
00:44:54,200 --> 00:44:56,640
Watch me, little Mochi.

541
00:44:56,720 --> 00:44:58,600
I'll show you who the real top dog is.

542
00:45:18,160 --> 00:45:19,600
<i>Thanks…</i>

543
00:45:22,920 --> 00:45:24,960
for pretending to be my boyfriend.

544
00:45:29,640 --> 00:45:33,200
Actually, I've told Rin many times,

545
00:45:33,280 --> 00:45:36,720
but he always had an excuse for himself.

546
00:45:37,960 --> 00:45:40,240
Why did you decide to do this?

547
00:45:47,160 --> 00:45:48,720
When I'm with Rin,

548
00:45:50,600 --> 00:45:52,000
I feel smaller.

549
00:45:54,440 --> 00:45:55,280
I just…

550
00:45:56,960 --> 00:45:58,600
wanted to get out of that feeling.

551
00:45:59,960 --> 00:46:02,560
So you chose to play the red flag
and take all the blame?

552
00:46:03,200 --> 00:46:07,400
The person who breaks up first
always looks worse anyway, right?

553
00:46:10,040 --> 00:46:12,560
This way, Rin can meet someone better.

554
00:46:57,640 --> 00:46:58,720
Hey, Khobfa!

555
00:47:01,920 --> 00:47:02,760
I'm sorry.

556
00:47:06,240 --> 00:47:07,680
You almost got unlucky again.

557
00:47:08,680 --> 00:47:09,840
Thanks.

558
00:47:13,000 --> 00:47:13,840
Wait.

559
00:47:14,720 --> 00:47:16,880
Why do you have this pen?

560
00:47:17,920 --> 00:47:19,000
This pen?

561
00:47:19,960 --> 00:47:21,040
Well, it's mine.

562
00:47:26,320 --> 00:47:27,480
That's it.

563
00:47:40,520 --> 00:47:42,240
So this pen isn't yours?

564
00:47:45,200 --> 00:47:47,320
No. It's Khobfa's.

565
00:47:47,400 --> 00:47:49,200
I borrowed it and forgot to return it.

566
00:47:52,680 --> 00:47:53,760
All good now, right?

567
00:47:53,840 --> 00:47:55,120
Give it back.

568
00:48:09,680 --> 00:48:10,760
Oh, I'm sorry!

569
00:48:14,800 --> 00:48:15,640
Damn it.

570
00:48:16,320 --> 00:48:17,440
Shit!

571
00:48:24,720 --> 00:48:26,840
Am I really the mystic heir?

572
00:48:28,120 --> 00:48:29,480
If this spellbook is real,

573
00:48:29,560 --> 00:48:31,520
then there has to be a way to undo it.

574
00:48:35,080 --> 00:48:37,960
"If the curse is not broken
before the cursed person's birthday,

575
00:48:38,040 --> 00:48:39,960
that person will meet their end."

576
00:48:41,120 --> 00:48:42,280
I'm screwed!

577
00:48:50,160 --> 00:48:52,440
<i>Give me Khobfa's contact details.</i>

578
00:48:57,600 --> 00:48:59,800
<i>The number you have dialed</i>
<i>cannot be reached at the moment.</i>

579
00:48:59,880 --> 00:49:02,120
Hey. Someone's hurt?

580
00:49:02,200 --> 00:49:03,760
Who's hurt?

581
00:49:09,320 --> 00:49:10,840
- Go check. Quick.
- Khobfa.

582
00:49:10,920 --> 00:49:11,760
Hurry up.

583
00:49:13,560 --> 00:49:14,560
Huh?

584
00:49:14,640 --> 00:49:18,120
- Hey, who's hurt?
- Is he hurt?

585
00:49:18,200 --> 00:49:20,480
- Is he okay?
- I bet this is serious.

586
00:49:22,840 --> 00:49:24,960
- Hey, listen up!
- Watch out!

587
00:49:26,040 --> 00:49:28,880
Rin!

588
00:49:42,640 --> 00:49:43,600
Are you okay?

589
00:49:47,040 --> 00:49:48,200
You're still alive.

590
00:50:16,000 --> 00:50:17,840
<i>What if I accidentally</i>
<i>used a curse from the spellbook</i>

591
00:50:17,920 --> 00:50:19,680
<i>to bring someone bad luck,</i>
<i>but I don't know how to undo it?</i>

592
00:50:19,760 --> 00:50:21,000
<i>What should I do, Mom?</i>

593
00:50:21,080 --> 00:50:23,520
<i>I believe everything has a way out.</i>

594
00:50:23,600 --> 00:50:26,560
<i>You just haven't found it yet, Rin.</i>

595
00:50:26,640 --> 00:50:28,080
Give it to me. I'll help you.

596
00:50:28,160 --> 00:50:29,680
<i>You're actually pretty cute.</i>

597
00:50:29,760 --> 00:50:31,520
But you complain a little too much.

598
00:50:31,600 --> 00:50:33,160
<i>Since when did you two get so close?</i>

599
00:50:33,240 --> 00:50:34,400
<i>Khobfa.</i>

600
00:50:35,000 --> 00:50:36,280
<i>Thanks.</i>

601
00:50:36,360 --> 00:50:38,000
<i>It's been a long time since anyone</i>

602
00:50:38,080 --> 00:50:40,160
<i>paid attention</i>
<i>to the little things about me.</i>

603
00:50:40,240 --> 00:50:42,280
Yes! Finally!

604
00:50:42,360 --> 00:50:44,200
I hope your bad luck is finally over.
